<h2>dig</h2>
<p>Another great tool is <code>dig</code>.</p>
<p>Here, I want to ask <a href="cloudflare.com">Cloudflare</a>'s DNS (<code>1.1.1.1</code>),
what mail server handles <a href="vg.no">vg</a>'s email:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>$ dig @1.1.1.1 vg.no MX

; &lt;&lt;&gt;&gt; DiG 9.18.18 &lt;&lt;&gt;&gt; @1.1.1.1 vg.no MX
; (1 server found)
;; global options: +cmd
;; Got answer:
;; -&gt;&gt;HEADER&lt;&lt;- opcode: QUERY, status: NOERROR, id: 24222
;; flags: qr rd ra; QUERY: 1, ANSWER: 5, AUTHORITY: 0, ADDITIONAL: 1

;; OPT PSEUDOSECTION:
; EDNS: version: 0, flags:; udp: 1232
;; QUESTION SECTION:
;vg.no.             IN  MX

;; ANSWER SECTION:
vg.no.          300 IN  MX  5 alt2.aspmx.l.google.com.
vg.no.          300 IN  MX  10 alt3.aspmx.l.google.com.
vg.no.          300 IN  MX  10 alt4.aspmx.l.google.com.
vg.no.          300 IN  MX  1 aspmx.l.google.com.
vg.no.          300 IN  MX  5 alt1.aspmx.l.google.com.

;; Query time: 26 msec
;; SERVER: 1.1.1.1#53(1.1.1.1) (UDP)
;; WHEN: Fri Aug 18 14:38:15 CEST 2023
;; MSG SIZE  rcvd: 152
</code></pre></div>

