<h2>Shodan</h2>
<p>I would normally use <code>curl</code> for gathering web server and TLS
certificate info, but there's a website (well, probably many) that
does this for you:</p>
<p><a href="https://www.shodan.io/search?query=skybert.net">shodan.io/search?query=skybert.net</a></p>
<p>The <code>curl</code> command I'd use is:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>$ curl -v https://skybert.net 2&gt;&amp;1 | \grep -E &#39;(subjectAltName|server|issuer):&#39;
*  subjectAltName: host &quot;skybert.net&quot; matched cert&#39;s &quot;skybert.net&quot;
*  issuer: C=US; O=Let&#39;s Encrypt; CN=R3
&lt; server: nginx
</code></pre></div>